---
title: French Labor Code & Corporate Charter on the Right to Disconnect
sourceType: statutory_statute
date: 2026-01-08
jurisdiction: France
language: en
register: statutory_legal
format: docx
---

Pursuant to French Labor Code Article L. 2242-17, every employee has a legally protected right to disconnect from all digital communication tools outside working hours.

No disciplinary action, penalty, or negative evaluation may be imposed on an employee who refuses to respond to emails, messages, or calls between 20:00 and 08:00 and on weekends.

Managers are strictly prohibited from requiring remote workers to maintain active chat presence or respond to urgent requests during statutory rest periods.
